<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fell in the week that ended April 23, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Apr 23 Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.92   +0.150    +0.921</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     6.18   -1.995    +2.675</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	432.99   -0.024    +2.115</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 132.10   -0.100   -29.600</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.78   -0.024    +2.115</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>					   Mar 97     Feb 97     Mar 96</p>
<p>M1					  68.32	68.43	59.02</p>
<p>M2					 391.84     392.57     389.03</p>
<p>M3					 506.02     500.30     475.88</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Mar	   Feb</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-16.69	-19.81</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     705.61	692.96</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    108.03	105.87</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
